## File Organization

### Directory Structure

```
libs/
├── services/                  # @helsoft/services
│   └── src/
│       ├── supabase/
│       │   └── supabase-client.ts   # initSupabase/getSupabase (shared client)
│       ├── dao/
│       │   ├── {feature-name}.dao.ts
│       │   └── ...
│       ├── services/
│       │   ├── {feature-name}.service.ts
│       │   ├── index.ts
│       │   └── ...
│       └── index.ts
└── hooks/                     # @helsoft/hooks
    └── src/
        ├── hooks/
        │   ├── use-{feature-name}.ts
        │   ├── index.ts
        │   └── ...
        └── index.ts
```

### Export Patterns

**DAO Exports**:

- DAOs should use `export class` or `export abstract class`

**Service Exports**:

- All services are exported through `src/services/index.ts`
- Services use `export abstract class` (or `export class` for instance-based)

**Hook Exports**:

- Hooks are exported through `src/hooks/index.ts`
- Hooks use `export function`

### Types

Follow `.agents/rules/types.mdc`.

- Multi-file / shared layer shapes (DAO DTOs, service results, hook return shapes, error codes) → co-located `{feature}.types.ts` (or `@helsoft/types` for cross-lib contracts)
- Do **not** export types from the DAO / service / hook implementation file
- Private / single-file types stay next to the implementation (or inline)

